# A line that ends with an operator goes on to the next line, unless that
# line starts like a statement (`p x`, `y = 2`, `return`) and is indented
# no deeper than the statement's first line: then the operand is missing,
# which is one error at the end of the line (it also closes a bracket left
# open there), and the next line is checked on its own. A value on such a
# line still continues the expression.
def main
  x = (1 +
  p   x
  y = 2 *
  p y
  z = [1, 2 +
  p z
  w = 1 +
    2
  v = w *
  w
  p v
end
